course: dictionary
lesson: 1201
title: Words that measure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bucketful is the amount one bucket can hold. «A bucketful of water» means as much water as a whole bucket will take, so it is a way of measuring, like a cupful.
explain: Read the words around it to check. «The hagfish lets out slime that becomes a bucketful of goo in seconds.» A whole bucket of goo is a lot, so the word tells you the amount is big, not one drop.
explain: Bucketful also has an informal meaning: a large amount. «Bucketfuls of rain» means a great deal of rain, as in «it rained buckets», not rain carried in a bucket. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A bucketful is a noun. One bucketful, two bucketfuls.
fact: «A bucketful of water» means the amount one bucket can hold.
fact: «Bucketfuls of rain» is informal and means a large amount of rain.
fact: In maths, a bucketful can be a unit of measure: if a bucket holds 10 litres, 3 bucketfuls hold 30 litres.
fact: The hagfish is an eel-shaped fish with no jaws, and it can make a bucketful of goo in seconds.
exercise: What does «a bucketful of water» mean? | a bucket of sand | an empty bucket | a bucket with a hole in it | *the amount one bucket can hold
exercise: The text says «bucketfuls of rain». What does bucketfuls mean here? | exactly ten litres | a rain cloud | *a large amount | a small drizzle
exercise: In maths, 3 bucketfuls hold 30 litres. How many litres does one bucketful hold? | 5 litres | *10 litres | 30 litres | 3 litres
test: Which word in «a bucketful of goo» tells you how much goo there is? | hagfish | slime | seconds | *bucketful
test: What is the plural of bucketful? | bucketful | buckets | bucketsful | *bucketfuls
exam: Sam reads «bucketfuls of rain» and asks what it means. Which answer is best? | Rain that has stopped | Rain caught in a bucket | A small drizzle | *A large amount of rain
